<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN to issue U.S. pref shares for SFB buy.</title>
<headline>ABN to issue U.S. pref shares for SFB buy.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch ABN AMRO said on Friday it would issue $750 million preference shares to help fund its acquisition of Standard Federal Bank.  </p>
<p>&quot;We intend to finance the transaction by means of an issue of $750 million preference shares in the United States through ABN AMRO North America Inc.,&quot; the Dutch bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The remainder will be financed from ABN AMRO Holding NV's existing means,&quot; ABN chairman Jan Kalff said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
